name: web
boss: crawler
flavor: A site you own, on the loopback that only means this machine.
brief: These probe a practice website the lab stands up on 127.0.0.1 -- your
brief: own, and the only address in range. `httpx` asks a URL what it is;
brief: `gobuster` guesses hidden paths from a wordlist. Same tools the pros
brief: point at real targets, aimed here where it is safe to learn them.
tools: httpx gobuster
lab: web
---
q: probe @url@ and show its status code, with `httpx`
a: httpx -u @url@ -sc -silent -nc
out: 200
ref: httpx
teach: httpx
hint: -u the url, -sc for the status code, -silent -nc for clean output
---
q: get the page title of @url@ with `httpx`
a: httpx -u @url@ -title -silent -nc
out: practice site
ref: httpx
teach: httpx
hint: -title asks for the <title> of the page
---
q: probe @url@ and show the web server it runs, with `httpx`
a: httpx -u @url@ -server -silent -nc
out: [Ss]erver|[Pp]ython|http
ref: httpx
teach: httpx
hint: -server reports the Server header
---
q: find the hidden page on @url@ with `gobuster`, using ``words.txt``
a: gobuster dir -u @url@ -w words.txt -q
out: secret
ref: gobuster
teach: gobuster
hint: dir mode, -u the url, -w the wordlist, -q for quiet output
seed: printf 'admin\nsecret\nlogin\nhello\n' > words.txt
---
q: run `gobuster` dir on @url@ with ``words.txt``, showing each path's status
a: gobuster dir -u @url@ -w words.txt
out: Status: 200
ref: gobuster
teach: gobuster
hint: without -q, gobuster prints the status of every path it finds
seed: printf 'admin\nsecret\nlogin\nhello\n' > words.txt
